      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Rubbish from the river
    number: 3
    heartsNeeded: 3
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - 'I mean it about rubbish. Old bottles, buttons, boots. Especially boots: people wrote their names in them, and the makers stamped theirs inside.'
    - Fish in the river near your farm long enough and it will give you a boot. It always does. Bring me one.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 11400000, guid: b8db9d30bff0d2a49994ba6dbd5fa3df, type: 2}
      amount: 1
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: A boot from the river
      questText: Grace wants an old boot fished out of the river. She says the maker's stamp could tell her something.
      reminder:
      - No boot yet? Keep fishing. The river is generous with boots. It is the fish it keeps to itself.
      thanks:
      - Perfect. Disgusting, and perfect.
      - 'Look, inside the heel. A stamp: ''Sterling & Sons Tannery''. A tannery. Do you know what tanneries poured into rivers? I am going to find out exactly.'
    choice:
      enabled: 0
      optionA: 
      replyA: []
      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Sterling & Sons
    number: 4
    heartsNeeded: 4
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - I found them. Sterling & Sons Tannery, upstream of your farm, ninety years ago. Victor Sterling's great-grandfather.
    - Tanneries soak leather in lime and chrome and things I won't say in front of Nia. All of it went into the river. For forty years.
    - So the tower didn't start this. It is only the newest chapter of a very old family habit.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 0
