  - title: Publish or wait
    number: 8
    heartsNeeded: 8
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - The book is finished. Every map, every tannery record, every boot. It is the best thing I have ever written.
    - If I publish, I will lose my job in the Sterling Wing. Probably my job anywhere. Emeka says we will manage. Nia says I can be a goalkeeper.
    - Or I keep the files somewhere safe and wait until someone can use them properly. A court. City hall. Someone braver than a history lecturer.
    - You found the boot. You have a vote.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 1
      optionA: Publish it
      replyA:
      - Then I will publish it. And I will give a lecture, in the plaza, free, to anybody who wants to come.
      - History is not for the Sterling Wing. It is for the people who live where it happened.
      flagsA:
      - grace_published
      - tower_file_maps
      optionB: Keep the files safe
      replyB:
      - Wait, then. A history that nobody reads can't be silenced, at least.
      - Here. Copies of everything, for you. Keep them somewhere damp-proof. Not in a barn. Please, not in a barn.
      flagsB:
      - grace_files_hidden
      - tower_file_maps
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: The plaza lecture
    number: 9
    heartsNeeded: 9
    path: 1
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - Did you see how many came? I counted sixty chairs, and then people sat on the fountain.
    - Walt asked the only rude question and it was a very good one. Nia sat in the front row holding the boot like a trophy.
    - The university has 'paused my contract'. The city paper has asked me to write a column. I think I have just traded forty students for forty thousand readers.
    happy: 1
    ask:
